meta {
  name: Scriptless Chaining
}

vars {
  baseUrl: https://dummyjson.com
  username: emilys
  password: emilyspass
}

assert {
  res.responseTime: lt 5000
}

docs {
  Scriptless request chaining + testing, no JavaScript anywhere.
  
  - **auth/Login** captures `token` and `userId` from the response (Tests tab → Set variables from response).
  - **users/Me** and **users/Carts** link to Login (Pre-request tab → Run first) *only when* `{{token}}` / `{{userId}}` are empty, so you can send them directly.
  - Every request is checked by the assertions in its Tests tab; the collection adds a response-time budget for all of them.
  
  Run it headless: `vegha run samples/scriptless-chaining`.
}
